<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72934" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλέκω</span></b> , impf. without augm. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄλεκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					11.150
				</span></i>
			 ; Iterat. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλέκεσκον</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλέεσκον</span>
			) <i><span class="en">
				19.135
			</span></i> :—pres.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλέσκω</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i> :—<i>ruin, destroy, kill,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always in last sense, and mostly of men, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ δ᾽ ἀλλήλους ὀλέκουσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					18.172
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				15.249
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				22.108
			</span></i>, etc. ; but in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				22.305
			</span></i>, of birds which <i>prey</i> on smaller birds, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ δέ τε τὰς ὀλέκουσιν ἐπάλμενοι</span> :
			in Philos., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίκτει τ᾽ ὀλέκει τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Emp.
					17.4
				</span></i>
			 :—
				Pass.
			, <i>perish, die,</i> esp. a violent death, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλέκοντο δὲ λαοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.10
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				16.17
			</span></i>.—Chiefly 
				Ep.
			, used by Trag. only in lyr., once in 
				Act.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί μ᾽ ὀλέκεις</span>; <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1285
			</span></i> (lyr.); twice in 
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλέκει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					563
				</span></i>
			(anap.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠλεκόμαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					1012
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.): later, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Jb.</u>
				10.16
			</span></i> :—
				Pass.
			, ib.<i><span class="en">
				17.1
			</span></i>.</div>
